ure central dominance.\n\nReason:  \nN: f3-e5 is a strong developing move that occupies the center, increases piece activity, and creates threats against f7 and d7. It prevents Black from comfortably playing ...e5 themselves and prepares potential attacks with minimal risk.\n\nAnswer: N: f3-e5"}
